            <ArticleTitle>[Pain in the knee as a first symptom of retroperitoneal space-occupying processes (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Knee complaints may be the first symptom of retroperitoneal space-occupying processes, as a result of compression of the femoral or obturator nerve. This differential diagnostic possibility is pointed out with reference to four case histories. The importance of CT examination as a part of the diagnostic procedure is emphasised.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
